# PIE – Privacy Policy

**Effective date:** October 15, 2026

PIE (“we,” “our,” or “the app”) is a news-reading application that helps users discover and read news stories. We respect your privacy and aim to collect as little personal information as possible.

## 1. Information We Collect

PIE is designed to operate without requiring users to create an account.

Depending on the features and configuration of the app, PIE may store settings locally on your device, such as notification preferences and selected news categories.

We do not intentionally collect your name, email address, phone number, precise location, or account credentials through the app.

## 2. News Sources and Internet Access

PIE retrieves news content from third-party news websites and RSS feeds. When the app requests content from these sources, those services may receive technical information such as your IP address and request details, in accordance with their own privacy policies.

PIE does not own or control the privacy practices of third-party news publishers.

## 3. Notifications

PIE may use background tasks to check for new articles and provide news notifications based on your settings. You can manage or disable notifications through the app or your device’s system settings.

## 4. Data Storage and Sharing

App preferences may be stored locally on your device. We do not sell personal information.

